raw_output:
```java
// Bad example: Vulnerable to SQL injection due to improper use of Statement
public class VulnerableServlet extends HttpServlet {
    protected void doPost(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response) {
        String userInput = request.getParameter("user_id");

        // Vulnerable: Concatenates user input directly into SQL query
        String query = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = " + userInput;

        try {
            Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:mysql://localhost/test");
            Statement stmt = conn.createStatement();
            ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery(query); // SQL injection point
        } catch (SQLException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

***
```java
// Good example: Uses PreparedStatement to prevent SQL injection
public class SecureServlet extends HttpServlet {
    protected void doPost(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response) {
        String userInput = request.getParameter("user_id");

        // Safe: Uses parameterized query to sanitize input
        String query = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?";

        try {
            Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:mysql://localhost/test");
            PreparedStatement pstmt = conn.prepareStatement(query);
            pstmt.setString(1, userInput); // Input is properly sanitized
            ResultSet rs = pstmt.executeQuery();
        } catch (SQLException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

